/-!
# The genuine 14.7.72 endgame

The original spans and quotient marking are kept throughout. The checked
centralization argument reduces the rank-two fixed-kernel exclusion to
[R,L] ≤ V, the earlier rank bound and the original local setup. An actual
Steinberg coordinate identification gives Z(S) = V and, after identification
of S with O₂(L) and the later T ≤ L, supplies the literal Ru1 constructor.

This module does not yet assert the complete source theorem. Generation from
14.7.66–71, construction and recognition of the marked parabolic quotient,
and the source involution/double-cover argument are separate obligations.
Their final assembly is retained here. In particular the coordinate interface
is an output to construct, not an assumption of the final book theorem.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, 14.7.72, printed pp.1075–1076 (PDF pp.1092–1093),
combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/
